            "review_text": "Tracy Bell\nHanoi, Vietnam41 contributions\n0\nsells the best peanut butter\nMay 2018 • Family\nYou may be sceptical at first because the place seems sketchy on the outside and a little hard to find, but the interior is very homey. The space is kind of small so groups of more than 10 people will be hard to fit. This restaurant is family-owned so the staff is super friendly. Some people don't speak English, but they understand what you're ordering. The food is fresh, cheap, healthy, and Vietnamese so you get a taste of the local vegetarian food dishes. You can also order ahead of time and pick the food up. They do not open on Mondays and open at 5PM for dinner so just keep that in mind if you are planning to come. If you are ever in need of peanut butter or black sesame spread, I get mine both of them here and they are delicious.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 21, 2018",
            "rating": 3.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
